# Payload audit: endpoints to review and the data actually used

## 1. What the boot chain requests (Lighthouse, mobile, throttled)

| # | Endpoint | Transfer | Notes |
| :--- | :--- | ---: | :--- |
| 1 | `GET /api/users/login` | 1,130 B | |
| 2 | `GET /api/screen` | 223 B | |
| 3 | `GET /api/global/settings` | 26,249 B | |
| 4 | `GET /api/users` | 212 B | |
| 5 | `GET /api/projects?with_metrics=0` | 104,227 B | |
| 6 | `GET /api/settings?codx_path=…` | 1,378 B | |
| 7 | `GET /api/projects/ai/models` | 8,434 B | |
| 8 | **`GET /api/chats?codx_path=…`** | **24,961,236 B** | 9,604 → 12,934 ms, blocks 9→12 |
| 9 | `GET /api/kanban` | 75,404 B | queued behind #8 |
| 10 | `GET /api/profiles` | 299,195 B | fetched again by `initProject()` |
| 11 | `GET /api/infra/hosts` `…/summary` `…/containers` `…/stacks` `…/images` `…/volumes` `…/networks` `…/events` | 356 + 624 + 44,296 + 3,638 + 16,353 + 16,745 + 2,384 + 13,970 B | ~98 KB, **fired at boot** (twice for `containers`) |

Total page weight: **71,094 KiB**; scripts 46.3 MB, *other* (JSON/XHR) 25.9 MB of which `/api/chats` is 24.9 MB.

## 2. Why `/api/chats` is 24.9 MB

```js
// src/store/chats.js
async loadChats() {
  const chats = await activeProject.$api.chats.list()   // GET /api/chats  (no params)
  chats.forEach(chat => registerChatSummary(state, chat))   // ← expects a SUMMARY
}
```

```js
// src/api/modules/chats.js
list:      (filters) => API.get(`/api/chats${qs}`)              // list  → should be summary
loadChat:  ({ id })  => API.get(`/api/chats?file_path=&id=${id}`) // single chat → full history
```

**The same endpoint serves two very different contracts.** The client treats the list as *summaries* (`registerChatSummary` only keeps the record + the "last message" preview and then sets `needsReload[chat.id] = true`). When a chat is opened, `loadUninitialized()` → `loadChat()` fetches `GET /api/chats?id=…` **again**.

So if the server returns full histories in the list:

1. The 25 MB is downloaded for nothing — the store immediately marks every chat for **reload on open** and downloads it a **second time**.
2. Every message object is turned into Vuex reactive state (`state.chats[id] = {...chat}`), which is what blows up script-evaluation time (`49.8 s` bootup, TBT `32.9 s`).

## 3. Data the client actually uses from the list response

| Consumer | Fields read |
| :--- | :--- |
| `chats.allChats` / `allTags` / `allPRs` / `allTemplates` | `id`, `tags`, `pr_view.from_branch`, `is_template` |
| `chats.channels`, `recentChats`, `activeChat` | `mode`, `name`, `updated_at`, `lastMessageAt` |
| `kanban.boardChats` / `sprintBoardChats` | `board`, `column`, `sprints`, `status`, `sort_index`, `pinned`, `parent_id`, `project_id`, `owner_project_id`, `profiles`, `users` |
| `TaskCard` / `TaskCardLite` | `task.messages` **scanned for the first image** (`messages?.find(m => m.images?.length)?.images[0]`), `updated_at`, `profiles`, `users` |
| `RecentChatsQuickAccess` | `messages` last `content`/`think`, truncated to **70 chars** |
| `AssistantChat` / `Assistant` | last message only |
| `ChatView`, `Chat` (after open) | the **full** `messages` array |

**Conclusion:** from the list endpoint the UI needs chat metadata + *one preview message* + *one thumbnail*. Everything else (`messages[]` with full `content`, `think`, `tool` events, `meta_data`, `request_messages`, `files`, `images` base64…) is dead weight.

## 4. Endpoints to review (priority order)

### P0 — `GET /api/chats` (list)

| Action | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Add a summary contract | Make `messages` carry **only the last message**, trimmed (e.g. 200 chars of `content`/`think`), or replace it with `last_message: { role, content, ts }`. |
| Add `messages_count` | The board/cards only need a count, not the array. |
| Add a thumbnail field | `thumbnail` (first image of the chat) so `TaskCard` stops scanning history. |
| Strip heavy sub-objects | `meta_data`, `pr_view.pull_requests`, `request_messages`, `log`, `session_id`, embedded `profiles`/`users` objects (send names only). |
| Paginate / filter | `?summary=1&limit=&offset=&board=` — or simply stop using it and call the endpoints that already do this (below). |
| Verify `codx_path` scoping | It receives `codx_path`; confirm it doesn't walk into sub-projects. |

Existing alternatives already implemented client-side that should replace it:
- `GET /api/chats/recent?page=&page_size=&user_id=&board=` → `chats.loadRecentChats()`
- `POST /api/chats/search` (paginated, summaries) → `chats.searchChats()`

### P1 — `GET /api/chats?id=…` (single chat)

| Action | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Keep full history here only | This is the only endpoint that should return `messages[]` complete. |
| Window it | `?messages_limit=&before=`, lazy-load older pages ("load all chat messages" is already a known slow path). |
| Return summary on writes | Ensure `PUT /api/chats?chat_only=1` (`saveChatInfo`) and `POST /api/chats/metadata` return the **summary**, not the full history — `updateChatInfo` is called on every drag/drop and status change. |

### P2 — `GET /api/profiles` (299 KB, fetched twice)

| Action | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Fields used | `name`, `description`, `avatar`, `path`, `chat_id`, `profiles` (nested) — the full prose/instructions body is **not** rendered in lists. |
| Action | Return a light list (`?fields=name,avatar,description,path,chat_id`) and load `ProfileViewer` bodies on demand; cache per project (it's already stored in `$state.profiles`). |

### P3 — `GET /api/infra/*` (~98 KB, 8 requests at boot)

| Action | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Cause | `src/views/infra/useInfra.js` is mounted because the **Infra panel is part of the restored desktop layout**, so Docker is queried at project activation. |
| Action | Trigger it only when the Infra panel becomes visible (`onDidActivePanelChange` / `IntersectionObserver`); `/api/infra/containers` is currently requested **twice**. |

### P4 — `GET /api/projects?with_metrics=0` (104 KB)

| Action | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Fields used | `project_id`, `project_name`, `codx_path`, `abs_project_path`, `project_icon`, `parent_id`, `project_dependencies`, `llm_model`, `embeddings_model`, `_metrics.last_update`. |
| Action | Verify `with_metrics=0` really strips metrics payloads; the sidebar only needs the fields above. |

### P5 — `GET /api/kanban` (75 KB)

| Action | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Action | Low priority, but it repeats chat ids per column; it is redundant with the chat list (`board`/`column`) and could be reduced to `boards → columns` only. |

## 5. How to measure before touching the server

```bash
# total size + per-chat breakdown
curl -s "$URL/api/chats?codx_path=$CODXP" | wc -c
curl -s "$URL/api/chats?codx_path=$CODXP" \
  | jq -r '.[] | [.id, (.messages|length), (.messages|map(.content//""|length)|add // 0)] | @tsv' \
  | sort -k3 -nr | head -20

# keys returned per chat (spot the heavy ones)
curl -s "$URL/api/chats?codx_path=$CODXP" | jq '.[0] | keys'

# what a single chat costs
curl -s "$URL/api/chats?codx_path=$CODXP&id=<chat-id>" | wc -c
```

Expected outcome: a handful of chats (long tasks / PR reviews / printed files) hold most of the MB, and `messages[].content` is the dominant field — the same data that is re-fetched when the chat is opened.

> Recap: the revert restores correctness (complete UI, chats awaited, board data present). The **real** speed-up has to come from making `GET /api/chats` return summaries — that alone removes ~25 MB from the critical path *and* stops every chat from being downloaded twice.

